speechtext:
It is required for the following improvements:
(1)	An extension to breakwater 300 feet in length by 25 feet wide in stone filled open faced cribwork, $22,000;
(2)	Repairs and improvements to town whtarf consisting of driving protection _ piles along west and north faces of outer end, $5,000;
(3)	Laying a double two-inch flooring over present flooring on outer end, $1,500; and renewing stringers and planking on older part of wharf, $2,500, or a total of $9,000;
(4)	To complete renewal of superstructure of older portion of east breakwater on a length of 140 feet by width of 27 feet which is in a dilapidated condition, replacing stringers, planking and cap pieces and reinforcing outer end, $2,000.

This vote is to be used
for:
(1)	Building of concrete parapet walls approximately six feet high across the ends of both piers' to prevent seas washing over same into freight shed;	;
(2)	Construction of four large creosoted pile dolphins near the corners of the two piers as protection to ships manoeuvering into berths;
(3)	The provision of floating fender logs moored to existing bollards by heavy chain, along four faces of piers.
The estimated cost is:
(1)	Parapet walls, $11,000.
(2)	4 creosoted pile dolphins. $26,000.
(3)	floating fender logs, $9,000.
